ainly: the pip resolution/install itself (no network or package downloads permitted — the recorded commands are what would run, not proof they succeed on a clean machine), `python -m venv` actually producing a working venv, the Windows .cmd and Start Menu entries actually executing (no Windows/pwsh here — content inspected only), GNOME trust/double-click behaviour (`gio set` argv recorded, not executed), and seeding the real HF model cache (deliberately skipped). | Tests: unchanged suites green at the time of the audit; fixes and re-verification in the next two entries.

2026-09-17 | scripts/manage_install.py | Defect: the manager's own launch path ignored the offline marker. On an install where `.oracle_offline` exists, `run_gui()` (reached via ./run_oracle_tts.sh, a documented launch path) spawned `['<repo>/.venv/bin/the-oracle', 'gui']` with HF_HUB_OFFLINE absent from the child environment — while the generated launcher and both desktop entries, written by the same installer, all export HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1. So the documented promise that an offline install "can never touch the network" held on the launcher/desktop paths but not on this one, and model loaders would reach for the network instead of the cache the bundle had seeded. Same family as the earlier `update --offline-bundle` drop. | Root-cause fix: run_gui() now sets HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1 when the marker is present, mirroring the launcher (deleting the marker remains the documented way to re-enable network fetches), with a comment stating why. Two regression tests added: test_run_path_exports_hf_hub_offline_on_offline_install (FAILS without the fix — recorded child env had no HF_HUB_OFFLINE) and test_run_path_leaves_offline_flag_unset_without_marker (an invariant guard that passes both before and after, pinning that the flag is not applied when there is no marker). | Verified live: probe now shows `HF_HUB_OFFLINE in child env : '1'` on the run path, matching the launcher. Suite: 895 passed / 0 failed / 0 errors (this tree); 894 passed / 1 skipped / 0 failed / 0 errors (pristine). Nothing pushed.

