2026-09-17 | Noticed, not actioned | `install()` runs the full doctor twice — once inside `bootstrap()` (unless --skip-doctor) and again at the end of `install()` — which loads Chatterbox on CPU each time. The second run is defensible (it validates the entrypoint after the launcher is installed) but the first is largely redundant work; leaving it alone because removing a verification step is a behaviour change beyond this pass's scope. Also theoretical and unfixed: a launcher path containing `%` (or, in the .desktop Exec quoting case, `"`/backtick/`$`) would need escaping that the freedesktop spec requires; no realistic HOME contains these, and spaces — the case that actually matters — are handled correctly and verified.

